{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/57479-exalted-the-wyld-hunt","id":57479,"title":"Exalted: the Wyld Hunt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-25T09:46:04-08:00","id":57479,"title":"Exalted: the Wyld Hunt","content":"I am hosting the following chronicle on Roll20.net (visit here for the official LFG page there: <a href=\"https://app.roll20.net/lfg/listing/11423/exalted-the-wyld-hunt\" target=\"_blank\">https://app.roll20.net/lfg/listing/1...-the-wyld-hunt</a>). Sessions will be conducted using standard real-time text chat and Roll20's dice roller, along with maps and any other visual tools (such as a combat wheel and so forth).<br /> <br /> *<br /> <br /> Starring agents of the Wyld Hunt in service of the Realm, this campaign chronicles their exploits and adventures both in the Threshold and on the Blessed Isle.The story begins just one year after the disappearance of the Scarlet Empress. The player-characters form one of the few teams fully devoted to the sacred Wyld Hunt. With darkness growing on all sides, your service is needed more than ever.<br /> <br /> Set against the foreboding backdrop of the Realm teetering on destruction, with seemingly insurmountable foes massing against the Dynasty, this chronicle will maintain a fairly dark and gritty tone -- without losing the larger-than-life heroics we know and love about Exalted. Prepare to be the underdogs who must band together and form the last line of defense against the mighty horrors of Creation and beyond. Also expect deeper questions of morality and justice, and delve into layers of mystery and secrets about the Realm, Anathema, and what it means to be a Dynast.<br /> <br /> Your adventures will consist of equal parts action, detective work, and intrigue as your commanders from the Wyld Hunt assign the team to a variety of missions ranging from simple hunts to complex investigations. Of course, there will be plenty of opportunities for character's to advance personal goals and to get caught up in larger events. Your place in the Wyld Hunt simply puts you on the front lines of destiny in these troubled times.<br /> <br /> *<br /> <br /> Character guidelines: All player-characters must be Dragon-Blooded in the service of the Wyld Hunt. Their reasons for serving can vary greatly, but all must have convincing reasons (whether noble or selfish). This campaign has five maximum player slots, one for each elemental aspect (there is a story reason for this that I cannot reveal yet). Currently, all of the aspects are open, but that will surely change soon. Thus, try to have a backup choice just in case. You can express your interest and ask questions and post basic character ideas here, or you can go to the roll20 page and post a character bio.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Limit charms to those listed in the Dragon-Blooded book. Charms from other supplements (Thousand Correct Actions, Dreams of the First Age, etc) might become available later in game. Sorcery spells can be drawn from the core rulebook and the White Treatise. For artifacts, if something you want is in a book other than the core rulebook, just ask me first. If it's reasonable and comes with a solid explanation, I'll probably approve it.<br /> <br /> *<br /> <br /> Player guidelines: Experienced Exalted players are preferred. On general principle, I have no problems at all with new Exalted players. I am a little wary of them for this particular chronicle however, because the barrier for entry is a bit higher (requiring catching up on two books worth of information, minimum), and because a Wyld Hunt -protagonist- group requires a slightly more nuanced understanding of the setting and lore to pull off. That said, if you are new to Exalted but are willing to go the extra mile to catch up, then I won't turn you away outright.<br /> <br /> Schedule: I would like to run this campaign every Sunday starting at 3:00 PM EST and ending around 8/9 PM or whenever we feel like stopping. Reliable attendance is essential, so please don't commit to it if you can't follow through.<br /> <br /> EDIT: House Rules: There's not too much here. I use the errata, but will probably require reminders on various changes therein. Beyond that, I use two house rules. Rule 1: Charms for favored, out-of-aspect abilities are treated as aspect ability charms (IE: no mote surcharge). Rule 2: The 1st, 2nd, and 3rd Excellencies are combined into one charm, and the user chooses which version to use when activating it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2098-christoph","user":"Christoph","date":". 01-25-2014, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2098-christoph","name":"Christoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T17:56:39-08:00","id":57791,"title":"","content":"I like the premise, just wish the schedule was different. Good luck with the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/385-savare","name":"Savare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}